:{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible: v4.8.dev.custom_build [a8a1405f5], v4.7.stable.arch_linux [5b4e0cb0f]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.8.dev (a8a1405f5) - Arch Linux #1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Sat, 18 Jul 2026 17:30:57 +0000 on Wayland - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 (nvidia; 610.43.03) - AMD Ryzen 5 2600 Six-Core Processor (12 threads) - 31.28 GiB memory - PulseAudio (44100 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nOn an exported array, when pressing `Tab` to focus on the next element, it focuses in the order of [ Drag button (hamburger icon), then delete button on the right, then the value input in the middle].\n\nVideo showing the issue:\nhttps://youtu.be/FmPm1yjG82Y\n\nIn my mind the order should be [Drag button, value input, delete button].\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Export an `Array` and add a few elements.\n2. Select the first element value input and press `Tab`.\n3. Observe how it jumps to the next element's drag button, instead of it's own delete button.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","e